    `the Authority has required the trustee-manager in writing to provide a copy of the register or part of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority required the trustee-manager in writing to provide it with a copy of the register or part of it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137K(4) the trustee-manager must send the Authority a copy of the register` MEANS
    IF `the body is the trustee-manager of a registered business trust or recognised business trust` AND `the Authority has required the trustee-manager in writing to provide a copy of the register or part of it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Authority may at any time in writing require the trustee-manager to provide it with a copy of the register or any part of the register and the trustee-manager must send the copy"

-- src:29237 | (4) The Authority may at any time in writing require the
