§ `s 137L: powers of the court with respect to non-compliance by substantial unitholders`

-- The orders of subsection (1), paragraphs (a) to (i). The kind matters in subsection (6), which carves out "an order restraining the exercise of voting rights" (paragraph (c));
-- fork register A7: paragraph (h), an order that the exercise of voting or other rights be disregarded, is not read as an order restraining their exercise.
DECLARE `s 137L(1) kind of order` IS ONE OF
    `s 137L(1)(a) an order restraining the substantial unitholder from disposing of any interest in the units`
    `s 137L(1)(b) an order restraining the holder or the person entitled to be the holder of the units from disposing of any interest in them`
    `s 137L(1)(c) an order restraining the exercise by any person of any voting or other rights attached to a unit`
    `s 137L(1)(d) an order directing the trustee-manager not to make payment, or to defer making payment, of any sum due in respect of a unit`
    `s 137L(1)(e) an order directing the sale of any or all of the units`
    `s 137L(1)(f) an order directing the trustee-manager not to register the transfer or transmission of units`
    `s 137L(1)(g) an order directing the Depository or any depository corporation not to register the transfer or transmission of units`
    `s 137L(1)(h) an order that any exercise of the voting or other rights attached to units be disregarded`
    `s 137L(1)(i) an order directing the trustee-manager or any other person to do or refrain from doing an act to secure compliance with another order`

-- The court "may, on the application of the Authority": a "Where ..." condition and an application, on a function named for a power. SPLIT-SITE (ii), fork line B3:
-- the grant limit of the ruling of 2026-11-12 answers NOTHING when the gate fails; the periods ruling (b) would answer JUST FALSE. The same answer serves every paragraph (a) to (i).
-- src:29257 | 137L.—(1) Where a person is or has been a substantial unitholder
-- src:29258 | of a registered business trust or recognised business trust and has
-- src:29259 | failed to comply with section 135, 136 or 137 as applied by
-- src:29260 | section 137J(1), a court may, on the application of the Authority,
-- src:29261 | whether or not that failure still continues, make one or more of the
-- src:29262 | following orders:
@ref s 137L(1) (src:29257-29262)
GIVEN
    `the person is or has been a substantial unitholder of the business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person, or has the person been, a substantial unitholder of the business trust?
    `the person has failed to comply with section 135, 136 or 137 as applied by section 137J(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person failed to comply with section 135, 136 or 137 as applied by section 137J(1) (whether or not that failure still continues)?
    `the Authority has applied to the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority applied to the court for an order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137L(1) the court has power to make one or more of the orders listed in the subsection` MEANS
    IF `the person is or has been a substantial unitholder of the business trust` AND `the person has failed to comply with section 135, 136 or 137 as applied by section 137J(1)` AND `the Authority has applied to the court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): SPLIT-SITE (ii) "Where a person is or has been a substantial unitholder of a registered business trust or recognised business trust and has failed to comply with section 135, 136 or 137 as applied by section 137J(1), a court may, on the application of the Authority"

-- src:29313 | (2) Any order made under this section may include such ancillary or
-- src:29314 | consequential provisions as the court thinks just.
@ref s 137L(2) (src:29313-29314)
GIVEN
    `an order has been made by the court under the section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court made an order under this section?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137L(2) the order may include ancillary or consequential provisions the court thinks just` MEANS
    IF `an order has been made by the court under the section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any order made under this section may include such ancillary or consequential provisions as the court thinks just"

-- Subsection (3): a sale order may carry a condition against a sale to a person who is, or would become, a substantial unitholder.
-- src:29318 | (3) An order made under this section directing the sale of any unit
-- src:29319 | may provide that the sale is to be made within such time and subject
-- src:29320 | to such conditions (if any) as the court thinks fit, including, if the
-- src:29321 | court thinks fit, a condition that the sale must not be made to a person
-- src:29322 | who is, or, as a result of the sale, would become a substantial
-- src:29323 | unitholder of the business trust.
@ref s 137L(3) (src:29318-29323)
GIVEN
    `an order directing the sale of a unit has been made under the section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court made an order directing the sale of a unit?
    `the court has made it a condition that the sale must not be made to a person who is, or would become, a substantial unitholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court made it a condition of the sale that it must not be made to a person who is, or as a result would become, a substantial unitholder of the business trust?
    `the buyer is, or as a result of the sale would become, a substantial unitholder of the business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the buyer, or would the buyer as a result of the sale become, a substantial unitholder of the business trust?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137L(3) the sale to the buyer is barred by the court's condition` MEANS
    IF `an order directing the sale of a unit has been made under the section` AND `the court has made it a condition that the sale must not be made to a person who is, or would become, a substantial unitholder` AND `the buyer is, or as a result of the sale would become, a substantial unitholder of the business trust`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "including, if the court thinks fit, a condition that the sale must not be made to a person who is, or, as a result of the sale, would become a substantial unitholder of the business trust"

-- Subsection (4): where a unit is not sold, the Authority may apply for directions (SPLIT-SITE (ii): a "Where" gate on a function named for a power; fork line B4).
-- src:29330 | (4) Where a unit is not sold in accordance with an order of the court
-- src:29331 | under this section, the Authority may apply to the court for directions,
-- src:29332 | including directions as to who the unsold unit is to vest in.
@ref s 137L(4) (src:29330-29332)
GIVEN
    `a unit has not been sold in accordance with an order of the court under the section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a unit not been sold in accordance with an order of the court under this section?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137L(4) the Authority may apply to the court for directions on the unsold unit` MEANS
    IF `a unit has not been sold in accordance with an order of the court under the section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): SPLIT-SITE (ii) "Where a unit is not sold in accordance with an order of the court under this section, the Authority may apply to the court for directions"

-- src:29336 | (5) The court, before making an order under this section and in
-- src:29337 | determining the terms of such an order, is to satisfy itself, so far as it
-- src:29338 | can reasonably do so, that the order would not unfairly prejudice any
-- src:29339 | person.
@ref s 137L(5) (src:29336-29339)
GIVEN
    `the court is about to make an order under the section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court about to make an order under this section?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137L(5) the court must first satisfy itself that the order would not unfairly prejudice any person` MEANS
    IF `the court is about to make an order under the section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before making an order under this section and in determining the terms of such an order"

-- Subsection (6): the bar. The court "is not to make an order ... other than an order restraining the exercise of voting rights, if it is satisfied" of (a) inadvertence, mistake or unawareness
-- and (b) that the failure ought to be excused. JUST TRUE is "barred". Outside the carve-out or the condition the answer is JUST FALSE ("the bar does not apply"): a bar is the provision's own question
-- (ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 2); the other reading, NOTHING, is listed in NOTES.md (marginal reading (b)). "(other than X)" is a site decided on its own words: fork line B5.
-- src:29343 | (6) The court is not to make an order under this section, other than
-- src:29344 | an order restraining the exercise of voting rights, if it is satisfied —
-- src:29346 | (a) that the failure of the person who is or has been a
-- src:29347 | substantial unitholder to comply as mentioned in
-- src:29348 | subsection (1) was due to the person’s inadvertence or
-- src:29349 | mistake or to the person not being aware of a relevant fact
-- src:29350 | or occurrence; and
-- src:29352 | (b) that in all the circumstances, the failure ought to be
-- src:29353 | excused.
@ref s 137L(6) (src:29343-29353)
GIVEN
    `the kind of order under section 137L` IS A `s 137L(1) kind of order` @desc Which kind of order is it (restrain disposal, restrain voting or other rights, withhold payment, direct a sale, stop registration of a transfer, disregard votes, or secure compliance)?
    `the court is satisfied that the failure was due to inadvertence or mistake or to not being aware of a relevant fact or occurrence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the failure to comply was due to the person's inadvertence or mistake or to the person not being aware of a relevant fact or occurrence?
    `the court is satisfied that in all the circumstances the failure ought to be excused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that in all the circumstances the failure ought to be excused?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137L(6) the court is not to make the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the kind of order under section 137L` EQUALS `s 137L(1)(c) an order restraining the exercise by any person of any voting or other rights attached to a unit`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than an order restraining the exercise of voting rights"
        IF `the court is satisfied that the failure was due to inadvertence or mistake or to not being aware of a relevant fact or occurrence` AND `the court is satisfied that in all the circumstances the failure ought to be excused`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is satisfied — (a) that the failure of the person who is or has been a substantial unitholder to comply as mentioned in subsection (1) was due to the person's inadvertence or mistake or to the person not being aware of a relevant fact or occurrence; and (b) that in all the circumstances, the failure ought to be excused"
        -- MARGINAL-READING (a): the bar is introduced with "if"; a failed "if" is taken as the text's no. The other reading is NOTHING.

-- Subsection (7): notice of the application (SPLIT-SITE (ii): "before making an order", a gate on a function named for a power; fork line B6).
-- src:29357 | (7) The court may, before making an order under this section, direct
-- src:29358 | that notice of the application be given to such persons as it thinks fit
-- src:29359 | or direct that notice of the application be published in such manner as
-- src:29360 | it thinks fit, or both.
@ref s 137L(7) (src:29357-29360)
GIVEN
    `an application for an order under the section has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application for an order under this section been made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137L(7) the court may direct that notice of the application be given or published` MEANS
    IF `an application for an order under the section has been made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): SPLIT-SITE (ii) "The court may, before making an order under this section, direct that notice of the application be given to such persons as it thinks fit"

-- src:29364 | (8) The court may rescind, vary or discharge an order made by it
-- src:29365 | under this section or suspend the operation of such an order.
@ref s 137L(8) (src:29364-29365)
GIVEN
    `an order has been made by the court under the section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court made an order under this section?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137L(8) the court may rescind, vary, discharge or suspend the order` MEANS
    IF `an order has been made by the court under the section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an order made by it under this section"

-- src:29369 | (9) Any person who contravenes an order made under this section
-- src:29370 | that is applicable to the person shall be guilty of an offence and shall
-- src:29371 | be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $50,000 and, in the
-- src:29372 | case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $5,000
-- src:29373 | for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after
-- src:29374 | conviction.
@ref s 137L(9) (src:29369-29374)
GIVEN
    `the person contravenes an order made under the section that is applicable to the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person contravene an order made under this section that is applicable to the person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137L(9) the person is guilty of an offence of contravening an order of the court` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes an order made under the section that is applicable to the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) the text says who is guilty ("Any person who contravenes an order made under this section that is applicable to the person"), not that anyone else is innocent

-- src:29369 | (9) Any person who contravenes an order made under this section
-- src:29370 | that is applicable to the person shall be guilty of an offence and shall
-- src:29371 | be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $50,000 and, in the
-- src:29372 | case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $5,000
-- src:29373 | for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after
-- src:29374 | conviction.
@ref 2 s 137L(9) (the penalty) (src:29369-29374)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 137L(9) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    -- a fine not exceeding $50,000 and a further fine not exceeding $5,000 a day after conviction; no imprisonment is stated, so 0
    Penalty OF 50000, 0, FALSE, 5000

DECLARE `s 137L action` IS ONE OF
    `s 137L contravene an order of the court made under the section`

-- src:29369 | (9) Any person who contravenes an order made under this section
-- src:29370 | that is applicable to the person shall be guilty of an offence and shall
-- src:29371 | be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $50,000 and, in the
-- src:29372 | case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $5,000
-- src:29373 | for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after
-- src:29374 | conviction.
@ref s 137L(9) (the prohibition as a regulative rule) (src:29369-29374)
GIVEN `the person` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 137L action`
`s 137L(9) the person shall not contravene an order of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the person`
    SHANT `s 137L contravene an order of the court made under the section`
    LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "contravened an order of the court made under section 137L that is applicable to the person (section 137L(9))"

-- Subsection (10): contempt is untouched.
