    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to the punishment of contempt of the court"; a contravention that is not a contempt is outside the subsection


§ `s 137M: power of a trustee-manager to require disclosure of beneficial interest in its voting units`

-- Subsection (1): a power, so a gate that fails answers NOTHING (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12). The chapeau is one function; paragraphs (a) and (b) say what the notice may ask.
-- src:29389 | 137M.—(1) The trustee‑manager of a registered business trust or
-- src:29390 | recognised business trust may by written notice require any
-- src:29391 | unitholder of the business trust within such reasonable time as is
-- src:29392 | specified in the notice —
@ref s 137M(1) (src:29389-29392)
GIVEN
    `the body is the trustee-manager of a registered business trust or recognised business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body the trustee-manager of a registered business trust or recognised business trust within section 137H?
    `the person is a unitholder of the business trust` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the keel's definition of "unitholder" answer for the person? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the requirement is made by written notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement made by written notice?
    `the notice specifies a reasonable time for the answer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice specify a time for the answer that is reasonable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137M(1) the trustee-manager may require the unitholder to give the information` MEANS
    IF `the body is the trustee-manager of a registered business trust or recognised business trust` AND (`the person is a unitholder of the business trust` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the requirement is made by written notice` AND `the notice specifies a reasonable time for the answer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The trustee-manager of a registered business trust or recognised business trust may by written notice require any unitholder of the business trust within such reasonable time as is specified in the notice"

-- src:29394 | (a) to inform it whether the unitholder holds any voting units
-- src:29395 | in the business trust as beneficial owner or as trustee; and
@ref s 137M(1)(a) (src:29394-29395)
GIVEN
    `the body is the trustee-manager of a registered business trust or recognised business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body the trustee-manager of a registered business trust or recognised business trust within section 137H?
    `the person is a unitholder of the business trust` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the keel's definition of "unitholder" answer for the person? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the requirement is made by written notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement made by written notice?
    `the notice specifies a reasonable time for the answer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice specify a time for the answer that is reasonable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137M(1)(a) the trustee-manager may require the unitholder to inform it whether the unitholder holds voting units as beneficial owner or as trustee` MEANS
    `s 137M(1) the trustee-manager may require the unitholder to give the information` `the body is the trustee-manager of a registered business trust or recognised business trust` `the person is a unitholder of the business trust` `the requirement is made by written notice` `the notice specifies a reasonable time for the answer`

-- src:29397 | (b) if the unitholder holds them as trustee, to indicate so far as
-- src:29398 | the unitholder can the persons for whom the unitholder
-- src:29399 | holds them (either by name or by other particulars
-- src:29400 | sufficient to enable those persons to be identified) and
-- src:29401 | the nature of their interest.
@ref s 137M(1)(b) (src:29397-29401)
GIVEN
    `the body is the trustee-manager of a registered business trust or recognised business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body the trustee-manager of a registered business trust or recognised business trust within section 137H?
    `the person is a unitholder of the business trust` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the keel's definition of "unitholder" answer for the person? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the requirement is made by written notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement made by written notice?
    `the notice specifies a reasonable time for the answer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice specify a time for the answer that is reasonable?
    `the unitholder holds voting units in the business trust as trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the unitholder hold the voting units in the business trust as trustee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137M(1)(b) the trustee-manager may require the unitholder who holds the units as trustee to indicate the persons for whom the unitholder holds them` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the unitholder holds voting units in the business trust as trustee`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the unitholder holds them as trustee"; a function named for a power whose "if" gate failed (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1)
        OTHERWISE `s 137M(1) the trustee-manager may require the unitholder to give the information` `the body is the trustee-manager of a registered business trust or recognised business trust` `the person is a unitholder of the business trust` `the requirement is made by written notice` `the notice specifies a reasonable time for the answer`

-- Subsection (2): a further notice to a person the first answers name. "Where ... the trustee-manager may": a gated power. SPLIT-SITE (ii), fork line B7:
-- the grant ruling of 2026-11-12 answers NOTHING when the gate fails; the periods ruling (b) would answer JUST FALSE.
