    `the body is the trustee-manager of a registered business trust or recognised business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body the trustee-manager of a registered business trust or recognised business trust within section 137H?
    `the trustee-manager has been informed that the person has an interest in voting units in the business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the trustee-manager been informed, pursuant to a notice given to any person under section 137M(1) or (2), that the person has an interest in any of the voting units in the business trust?
    `the requirement is made by written notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement made by written notice?
    `the notice specifies a reasonable time for the answer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice specify a time for the answer that is reasonable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137M(2)(a) the trustee-manager may require the other person to inform it whether the person holds the interest as beneficial owner or as trustee` MEANS
    `s 137M(2) the trustee-manager may require the other person to give the information` `the body is the trustee-manager of a registered business trust or recognised business trust` `the trustee-manager has been informed that the person has an interest in voting units in the business trust` `the requirement is made by written notice` `the notice specifies a reasonable time for the answer`

-- src:29415 | (b) if that other person holds it as trustee, to indicate so far as
-- src:29416 | that other person can the persons for whom that other
-- src:29417 | person holds it (either by name or by other particulars
-- src:29418 | sufficient to enable them to be identified) and the nature of
