    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person holds that interest as trustee`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if that other person holds it as trustee"; a function named for a power whose "if" gate failed (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1)
        OTHERWISE `s 137M(2) the trustee-manager may require the other person to give the information` `the body is the trustee-manager of a registered business trust or recognised business trust` `the trustee-manager has been informed that the person has an interest in voting units in the business trust` `the requirement is made by written notice` `the notice specifies a reasonable time for the answer`

-- Subsection (3): the question of control by agreement or arrangement; "if so" gives the particulars. A power, so an unmet "if so" answers NOTHING (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1).
