        OTHERWISE `s 137M(3) the trustee-manager may require the unitholder to inform it whether the voting rights are subject to an agreement or arrangement` `the body is the trustee-manager of a registered business trust or recognised business trust` `the person is a unitholder of the business trust` `the requirement is made by written notice` `the notice specifies a reasonable time for the answer`

-- Subsection (4): the content and delivery of the notice are the Authority's to prescribe, so what they are is an input (the same pattern as section 133(3)(a)).
-- src:29438 | (4) The notice referred to in subsection (1), (2) or (3) must contain
-- src:29439 | such other information as the Authority may prescribe, and the
-- src:29440 | delivery of such notice must comply with such requirements as the
-- src:29441 | Authority may prescribe.
@ref s 137M(4) (src:29438-29441)
GIVEN
    `the Authority has prescribed other information and requirements for the notice and its delivery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed other information that the notice must contain, and requirements for its delivery?
    `the notice contains the information the Authority prescribes and its delivery complies with the requirements the Authority prescribes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice contain the other information the Authority prescribes, and does its delivery comply with the requirements the Authority prescribes?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137M(4) the notice contains the other information the Authority prescribes and is delivered as it prescribes` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Authority has prescribed other information and requirements for the notice and its delivery`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "such other information as the Authority may prescribe"
        IF `the notice contains the information the Authority prescribes and its delivery complies with the requirements the Authority prescribes`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must contain such other information as the Authority may prescribe, and the delivery of such notice must comply with such requirements as the Authority may prescribe"

-- Subsection (5): the duty to comply. It is class-limited ("Any person to whom a notice is issued"), so a person with no notice is outside it: NOTHING.
-- Whether a notice that fails subsection (4) still binds is a question the text does not answer (fork register B8): the duty is read as triggered by the issue of the notice.
-- src:29445 | (5) Any person to whom a notice is issued under subsection (1), (2)
-- src:29446 | or (3) must comply with that notice.
