`s 137M(5) the person must comply with the notice` MEANS
    IF `a notice has been issued to the person under section 137M(1), (2) or (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person to whom a notice is issued under subsection (1), (2) or (3)"

DECLARE `s 137M action` IS ONE OF
    `s 137M comply with the notice`

-- "Within such reasonable time as is specified in the notice": the number of days the notice allows is an input and the rule's window.
-- src:29389 | 137M.—(1) The trustee‑manager of a registered business trust or
-- src:29390 | recognised business trust may by written notice require any
-- src:29391 | unitholder of the business trust within such reasonable time as is
-- src:29392 | specified in the notice —
-- src:29394 | (a) to inform it whether the unitholder holds any voting units
-- src:29395 | in the business trust as beneficial owner or as trustee; and
-- src:29397 | (b) if the unitholder holds them as trustee, to indicate so far as
-- src:29398 | the unitholder can the persons for whom the unitholder
-- src:29399 | holds them (either by name or by other particulars
-- src:29400 | sufficient to enable those persons to be identified) and
-- src:29401 | the nature of their interest.
-- src:29405 | (2) Where the trustee‑manager of a registered business trust or
-- src:29406 | recognised business trust is informed pursuant to a notice given to any
-- src:29407 | person under subsection (1) or under this subsection that any other
-- src:29408 | person has an interest in any of the voting units in the business trust,
-- src:29409 | the trustee‑manager may by written notice require that other person
-- src:29410 | within such reasonable time as is specified in the notice —
-- src:29412 | (a) to inform it whether that other person holds that interest as
-- src:29413 | beneficial owner or as trustee; and
-- src:29415 | (b) if that other person holds it as trustee, to indicate so far as
-- src:29416 | that other person can the persons for whom that other
-- src:29417 | person holds it (either by name or by other particulars
-- src:29418 | sufficient to enable them to be identified) and the nature of
-- src:29419 | their interest.
-- src:29423 | (3) The trustee‑manager of a registered business trust or recognised
-- src:29424 | business trust may by written notice require any unitholder of the
-- src:29425 | business trust to inform it, within such reasonable time as is specified
-- src:29426 | in the notice, whether any of the voting rights carried by any voting
-- src:29427 | units in the business trust held by the unitholder are the subject of an
-- src:29428 | agreement or arrangement under which another person is entitled to
-- src:29433 | control the unitholder’s exercise of those rights and, if so, to give
-- src:29434 | particulars of the agreement or arrangement and the parties to it.
-- src:29438 | (4) The notice referred to in subsection (1), (2) or (3) must contain
-- src:29439 | such other information as the Authority may prescribe, and the
-- src:29440 | delivery of such notice must comply with such requirements as the
-- src:29441 | Authority may prescribe.
-- src:29445 | (5) Any person to whom a notice is issued under subsection (1), (2)
-- src:29446 | or (3) must comply with that notice.
@ref s 137M(5) (the duty as a regulative rule) (src:29389-29446)
GIVEN
    `the person` IS A Party
    `the time the notice specifies, in days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the notice is the time that the notice specifies for the answer?
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 137M action`
`s 137M(5) the person must comply with the notice within the time it specifies` MEANS
    PARTY `the person`
    MUST `s 137M comply with the notice`
    WITHIN `the time the notice specifies, in days`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "the notice was not complied with within the time it specified (section 137M(5))"

-- Subsection (6): the trustee-manager's duty to inscribe, "Whenever" counting as "where" (the ruling of 2026-11-05, (c)): a failed gate answers JUST FALSE.
-- src:29450 | (6) Whenever the trustee‑manager of a registered business trust or
-- src:29451 | recognised business trust receives information from a person
-- src:29452 | pursuant to a requirement imposed on the person under this section
-- src:29453 | with respect to units held by a unitholder of the business trust, it is
-- src:29454 | under an obligation to inscribe against the name of that unitholder in a
-- src:29455 | separate part of the register kept by it under section 137K —
-- src:29457 | (a) the fact that the requirement was imposed and the date on
-- src:29458 | which it was imposed; and
-- src:29460 | (b) the information received pursuant to the requirement.
@ref s 137M(6) (src:29450-29460)
GIVEN
    `the body is the trustee-manager of a registered business trust or recognised business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body the trustee-manager of a registered business trust or recognised business trust within section 137H?
    `the trustee-manager has received information from a person pursuant to a requirement imposed under section 137M with respect to units held by a unitholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the trustee-manager received information from a person, pursuant to a requirement imposed on the person under section 137M, with respect to units held by a unitholder of the trustee-manager?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137M(6) the trustee-manager must inscribe the fact of the requirement, its date and the information in a separate part of the register` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the body is the trustee-manager of a registered business trust or recognised business trust`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the trustee-manager of a registered business trust or recognised business trust"; the body is not one
        IF `the trustee-manager has received information from a person pursuant to a requirement imposed under section 137M with respect to units held by a unitholder`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Whenever the trustee-manager of a registered business trust or recognised business trust receives information from a person pursuant to a requirement imposed on the person under this section with respect to units held by a unitholder of the business trust"

-- src:29464 | (7) Section 137K applies in relation to the part of the register
-- src:29465 | referred to in subsection (6) as it applies in relation to the remainder
-- src:29466 | of the register and as if references to subsection (1) of that section
-- src:29467 | included references to subsection (6).
@ref s 137M(7) (src:29464-29467)
GIVEN
    `the part of the register is the separate part referred to in section 137M(6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the part of the register the separate part that section 137M(6) refers to?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137M(7) section 137K applies to the separate part of the register` MEANS
    IF `the part of the register is the separate part referred to in section 137M(6)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the part of the register referred to in subsection (6)"

-- src:29471 | (8) Any person who —
-- src:29473 | (a) intentionally or recklessly contravenes subsection (5); or
-- src:29475 | (b) in purported compliance with subsection (5), provides any
-- src:29476 | information which the person knows is false or misleading
-- src:29477 | in a material particular or is reckless as to whether it is,
-- src:29479 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall —
-- src:29481 | (c) in the case of an individual, be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:29482 | not exceeding $250,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- src:29483 | exceeding 2 years or to both and, in the case of a continuing
-- src:29488 | offence, to a further fine not exceeding $25,000 for every
-- src:29489 | day or part of a day during which the offence continues
-- src:29490 | after conviction; or
-- src:29492 | (d) in the case of a corporation, be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:29493 | not exceeding $250,000 and, in the case of a continuing
-- src:29494 | offence, to a further fine not exceeding $25,000 for every
-- src:29495 | day or part of a day during which the offence continues
-- src:29496 | after conviction.
@ref s 137M(8) (src:29471-29496)
GIVEN
    `the person contravened section 137M(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person contravene section 137M(5)?
    `the contravention was intentional or reckless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention intentional or reckless?
    `the person in purported compliance with section 137M(5) provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In purported compliance with section 137M(5), did the person provide information that is false or misleading in a material particular?
    `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person know that the information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was the person reckless as to whether it was?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137M(8) the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (8)` MEANS
    IF ((`the person contravened section 137M(5)` AND `the contravention was intentional or reckless`) OR (`the person in purported compliance with section 137M(5) provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` AND `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) the text says who is guilty ("intentionally or recklessly contravenes subsection (5)" or "provides any information which the person knows is false or misleading in a material particular or is reckless as to whether it is"), not that anyone else is innocent

@ref s 137M(8) (the penalty) (src:29471-29496)
GIVEN
    `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an individual (a natural person)?
    `the person is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a corporation (as section 2(1) defines "corporation")?
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 137M(8) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is an individual`
        THEN JUST (Penalty OF 250000, 24, TRUE, 25000)  -- a fine not exceeding $250,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years (24 months) or both; a further fine not exceeding $25,000 a day after conviction
        IF `the person is a corporation`
        THEN JUST (Penalty OF 250000, 0, FALSE, 25000)  -- a fine not exceeding $250,000, no imprisonment is stated, so 0; a further fine not exceeding $25,000 a day after conviction
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of an individual" and "in the case of a corporation" are the only cases the paragraphs name

-- src:29500 | (9) Any person who —
-- src:29502 | (a) contravenes subsection (5); or
-- src:29504 | (b) in purported compliance with subsection (5), provides any
-- src:29505 | information which is false or misleading in a material
-- src:29506 | particular,
-- src:29508 | in circumstances other than as set out in subsection (8) shall be guilty
-- src:29509 | of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:29510 | $25,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- src:29511 | exceeding $2,500 for every day or part of a day during which the
-- src:29512 | offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 137M(9) (src:29500-29512)
GIVEN
    `the person contravened section 137M(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person contravene section 137M(5)?
    `the contravention was intentional or reckless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention intentional or reckless?
    `the person in purported compliance with section 137M(5) provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In purported compliance with section 137M(5), did the person provide information that is false or misleading in a material particular?
    `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person know that the information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was the person reckless as to whether it was?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137M(9) the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (9)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person contravened section 137M(5)` OR `the person in purported compliance with section 137M(5) provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) the text says who is guilty ("contravenes subsection (5)"), not that anyone else is innocent
        IF ((`the person contravened section 137M(5)` AND `the contravention was intentional or reckless`) OR (`the person in purported compliance with section 137M(5) provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` AND `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was`))
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): SPLIT-SITE (i) "in circumstances other than as set out in subsection (8)": a case within subsection (8) is carved out of this one (a named complement)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 137M(9) (the penalty) (src:29500-29512)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 137M(9) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    -- a fine not exceeding $25,000 and a further fine not exceeding $2,500 a day after conviction; no imprisonment is stated, so 0
    Penalty OF 25000, 0, FALSE, 2500

-- src:29524 | (11) No proceedings shall be instituted against a person for an
-- src:29525 | offence under this section after ––
-- src:29527 | (a) a court has made an order against the person for the
-- src:29528 | payment of a civil penalty under section 137ZD in respect
-- src:29529 | of the same contravention; or
-- src:29531 | (b) the person has entered into an agreement with the
-- src:29532 | Authority to pay, with or without admission of liability, a
-- src:29533 | civil penalty under section 137ZD(4), in respect of the
-- src:29534 | same contravention.
@ref s 137M(11) (src:29524-29534)
GIVEN
    `a court has made an order for the payment of a civil penalty under section 137ZD for the same contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court made an order against the person for the payment of a civil penalty under section 137ZD for the same contravention?
    `the person has agreed with the Authority to pay a civil penalty under section 137ZD(4) for the same contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person entered into an agreement with the Authority to pay, with or without admission of liability, a civil penalty under section 137ZD(4) for the same contravention?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137M(11) no proceedings may be instituted for an offence under section 137M` MEANS
    IF `a court has made an order for the payment of a civil penalty under section 137ZD for the same contravention` OR `the person has agreed with the Authority to pay a civil penalty under section 137ZD(4) for the same contravention`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No proceedings shall be instituted against a person for an offence under this section after"
    -- MARGINAL-READING (b): the bar is limited by its own wording ("after"); outside the limit the other reading is NOTHING.

-- Subsection (10): the defence. It is limited to the paragraphs that are contraventions of subsection (5), (8)(a) and (9)(a), and is a defence "if the person proves"
-- one of two things. When neither is proved the answer is JUST FALSE, worded "this section gives no defence on these facts" (NOTHINGBURGER, (b)).
-- src:29516 | (10) A person shall not be guilty of an offence under
-- src:29517 | subsection (8)(a) or (9)(a) if the person proves that the information
-- src:29518 | in question was already in the possession of the trustee‑manager of
-- src:29519 | the registered business trust or recognised business trust, or that the
-- src:29520 | requirement to give it was for any other reason frivolous or vexatious.
@ref s 137M(10) (src:29516-29520)
GIVEN
    `the offence charged is one under section 137M(8)(a) or (9)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence charged one under section 137M(8)(a) or (9)(a) (a contravention of section 137M(5)), and not one for false or misleading information?
    `the person proves that the information in question was already in the possession of the trustee-manager` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person prove that the information in question was already in the possession of the trustee-manager?
    `the person proves that the requirement to give the information was for any other reason frivolous or vexatious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person prove that the requirement to give the information was, for any other reason, frivolous or vexatious?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137M(10) the person is not guilty of an offence under subsection (8)(a) or (9)(a)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offence charged is one under section 137M(8)(a) or (9)(a)`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence under subsection (8)(a) or (9)(a)"
        IF `the person proves that the information in question was already in the possession of the trustee-manager` OR `the person proves that the requirement to give the information was for any other reason frivolous or vexatious`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the person proves that the information in question was already in the possession of the trustee-manager of the registered business trust or recognised business trust, or that the requirement to give it was for any other reason frivolous or vexatious"; this section gives no defence on these facts

